# Pictures go to wmde-viewer, assigned only the types that MimeType= of its own desktop
# entry declares: claiming a type the application cannot decode replaces the ordinary
# "open with" dialog with an error. It takes every type it declares, aliases written in
# their canonical shared-mime-info form (image/x-icon is vnd.microsoft.icon, image/heic is
# heif; image/x-qoi is no registered type and gets no key), compressed SVG and the thirteen
# camera RAW types among them. wmde-photos, which opened those two before, is retired.
image/jpeg=fun.wmde.Viewer.desktop
image/png=fun.wmde.Viewer.desktop
image/webp=fun.wmde.Viewer.desktop
image/gif=fun.wmde.Viewer.desktop
